      "content": "It is a cruel but temporary lie to think you can never be someone good again, because that judgment is yours placing on yourself rather than anyone else's view of you. No one will truly hide from the cracks once they look at you, and pretending to be the golden child is only hurting you further by locking you in a prison you don't deserve. Your worth was never conditional on having no flaws, and the only way forward is to let go of the perfectionists' burden so you can become a complete, human being.",
